['Comparatives that state preferences', q{<em>"Early and ugly beats late and polished."</em> — [adjective + adjective] beats [adjective + adjective]: the comparative doing preference work with zero hedging. Sarah\'s whole style is in that grammar. Mirror it when confirming: <em>"early and ugly it is"</em> — the it-is echo locks the preference in as an agreement.}, q{"Early and ugly beats late and polished."——[形容词+形容词] beats [形容词+形容词]：比较级完成偏好表达，零对冲。Sarah 的整个风格都在这个语法里。确认时模仿它："early and ugly it is"——it-is 回声把偏好锁定为双方共识。}],
