title => 'Asking "Silly" Questions Well', cn => '把"傻问题"问得体面',
focus => 'The four-part question frame: context, attempt, the gap, and the offer to close the loop',
scenario => [
q{Week one, and you are drowning in things you do not understand. The team keeps saying <strong>"ask anything!"</strong> — but you have noticed the difference between <strong>questions that make people lean in and questions that make people check their phones.</strong> Today you watch Daniel K ask a "basic" question and get a twelve-minute whiteboard session for his trouble. <strong>His questions have a shape.</strong>},
q{第一周，你泡在不懂的东西里。团队一直说 <strong>"随便问！"</strong>——但你注意到了"让人身体前倾的问题"和"让人掏出手机的问题"的区别。今天你看到 Daniel K 问了一个"基础"问题，换来一场 12 分钟的白板讲解。<strong>他的问题是有形状的。</strong>},
q{The shape: <strong>context (what I am trying to do), attempt (what I tried), the gap (what specifically I do not understand), and the loop-close (what I will do with the answer)</strong>. "Silly" is not about the knowledge level of the question — <em>it is about the homework visibly missing.</em>},
q{形状是：<strong>背景（我要做什么）、尝试（我试了什么）、缺口（具体哪里不懂）、闭环（答案我会怎么用）</strong>。"傻"与问题的知识层级无关——<em>关键在于显而易见地没做功课。</em>},
],
dialogue => [
['You (New Joiner)', q{(to yourself, studying Daniel\'s question) Dissecting it. <strong>Context first:</strong> "I am trying to add the retry logic to the ingestion job" — <em>he anchored it to a real task, not curiosity in the abstract.</em>}, q{（研究 Daniel 的问题）解剖一下。<strong>先给背景：</strong>"我在给 ingestion job 加重试逻辑"——<em>他把它锚定在真实任务上，而不是抽象的好奇。</em>}],
['Daniel K (Senior Dev)', q{— and here is the part I keep tripping on. <strong>What I tried:</strong> the naive approach — wrap the whole batch in a try-catch and re-run it. <strong>What happens:</strong> duplicates downstream, because the successful rows get re-ingested. <strong>So my actual gap is:</strong> is idempotency the job\'s responsibility or the framework\'s?}, q{——这是我反复栽跟头的地方。<strong>我试过的：</strong>最朴素的做法——整个 batch 包 try-catch 重跑。<strong>结果：</strong>下游出现重复，因为已成功的行被再次摄取。<strong>所以我真正的缺口是：</strong>幂等性是作业的责任还是框架的责任？}],
['Elena (Tech Lead)', q{Twelve minutes for that one, and worth every minute — <em>because you brought the failed attempt with you.</em> The question behind your question is the right one: it is the framework\'s job, and you just found the gap in our onboarding doc.}, q{这个问题值得 12 分钟——<em>因为你把失败的尝试一起带来了。</em>你问题背后的问题才是对的：责任在框架——而你刚发现了我们入职文档的一个缺口。}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Reverse-engineering the anatomy. <strong>Part one, context:</strong> one sentence — "I am doing X, part of Y." <strong>Part two, attempt:</strong> what I tried and what actually happened — <em>the failure is the credential</em>, it proves the question is earned.}, q{反向解剖。<strong>第一部分，背景：</strong>一句话——"我在做 X，属于 Y。<strong>第二部分，尝试：</strong>我试了什么、实际发生了什么——<em>失败本身就是资格证明</em>，它证明这个问题是挣来的。}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{<strong>Part three, the gap — and this is where mine usually go wrong:</strong> not "I do not understand the ingestion framework" (a whole book), but <em>"is idempotency the job\'s responsibility or the framework\'s?"</em> — one decision-sized question. <strong>Part four, the loop:</strong> "whatever the answer is, I will add it to the onboarding doc." — <em>the answer becomes a wiki entry, and the asker becomes an author.</em>}, q{<strong>第三部分，缺口——我的问题通常死在这里：</strong>不是"我不懂 ingestion 框架"（一整本书），而是<em>"幂等性是作业的责任还是框架的？"</em>——一个决策尺寸的问题。<strong>第四部分，闭环：</strong>"无论答案是什么，我会写进入职文档。"——<em>答案变成 wiki 条目，提问者变成作者。</em>}],
['Priya (Delivery)', q{You two are making this look easy. Wei — <strong>your turn in the wild:</strong> you have a real one queued, I saw it.}, q{你们俩把这讲得太轻松了。Wei——<strong>轮到你实战了：</strong>我看到你排着一个真问题。}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Yes — here goes. <strong>Context:</strong> I am building the churn dashboard view, part of the spike Elena gave me. <strong>Attempt:</strong> I joined the customer table to the events table on customer ID and the query ran nine minutes, so I tried a window function instead — <strong>it returned in four seconds but the totals differ by 0.3%</strong>. <strong>My gap:</strong> is the 0.3% double-counting in the join, or legitimate reactivation events the window function drops?}, q{好——来了。<strong>背景：</strong>我在做流失仪表盘视图，Elena 给的 spike 任务。<strong>尝试：</strong>客户表按 ID 连接事件表，查询跑了 9 分钟；改用窗口函数——<strong>4 秒返回，但总额差了 0.3%</strong>。<strong>缺口：</strong>这 0.3% 是连接中的重复计数，还是窗口函数漏掉的合法"再激活"事件？}],
['Elena (Tech Lead)', q{Stop — <em>that is a senior analyst\'s question.</em> You have isolated the discrepancy to two mechanisms and asked which one owns it. Answer: it is double-counting; reactivations have a flag, join on the flag. <strong>And yes — doc entry, you write it.</strong>}, q{停——<em>这是资深分析师级别的问题。</em>你把偏差隔离到两种机制，并问出哪个该负责。答案：是重复计数；再激活有标志位，按标志位连接。<strong>而且没错——文档条目，你来写。</strong>}],
],
phrases => [
['Anchor', q{I am trying to add retry logic to the ingestion job.}, q{我在给 ingestion job 加重试逻辑。}, q{Anchor the question to a live task — abstract curiosity invites abstract answers.}],
['Credential', q{What I tried: the naive approach — and it duplicates downstream.}, q{我试过：最朴素的做法——结果下游重复。}, q{The failed attempt is your proof of homework. No attempt, no question — go back and try the naive version first.}],
['Size', q{My actual gap is: is it the job\'s or the framework\'s?}, q{我真正的缺口是：是作业的责任还是框架的？}, q{One decision-sized question. If your gap is a whole textbook chapter, you have not finished digging.}],
['Close', q{Whatever the answer is, I will add it to the onboarding doc.}, q{无论答案是什么，我都会写进入职文档。}, q{The loop-close that turns asking into contributing — and makes people want you to ask more.}],
