['You (New Joiner)', q{Testing the routing question on Marco first. <em>"Marco — if I had a question about the data retention policy at 4 PM on a Friday, who do I ask, and how would they want to be asked?"</em>}, q{先在 Marco 身上测试路由问题。<em>"Marco——周五下午 4 点我有一个数据保留政策的问题，该问谁？他们希望被怎么问？"</em>}],
['Marco (Buddy)', q{<strong>Ask Elena — but not at 4 PM Friday.</strong> Policy questions go to her in writing, weekdays, before noon. <em>She answers writing better than talking,</em> and Friday-afternoon policy debates are how bad decisions get made. <strong>Who to ask is half the answer; when and how is the other half.</strong>}, q{<strong>问 Elena——但别在周五下午 4 点。</strong>政策类问题书面提、工作日、中午前。<em>她读文字的反应比口头好，</em>而周五下午的政策辩论正是坏决策的生产线。<strong>问谁只是答案的一半；何时问、怎么问是另一半。</strong>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{Adding a fifth column then: <strong>how they want to be asked.</strong> Elena: written, before noon. That column just saved my first impression. <em>Next test: the two Daniels.</em>}, q{那就加第五栏：<strong>他们希望被怎么问。</strong>Elena：书面、中午前。这一栏刚刚拯救了我的第一印象。<em>下一个测试：两位 Daniel。</em>}],
['Daniel B (Senior Dev)', q{Routing question? Fire away.}, q{路由问题？问吧。}],
