['The emphatic "that is who" close', q{<em>"If learning it from the meeting would feel like an ambush — that is who."</em> — the conditional setup lands on the emphatic <strong>that is who</strong>, which converts a rule into a memorable answer. The same close works for any definition you are asked to give: <em>"if it would embarrass the team in the retro — that is the thing to flag."</em>}, q{"If learning it from the meeting would feel like an ambush — that is who."——条件句铺垫后落在强调的 <strong>that is who</strong> 上，把规则变成难忘的答案。任何被要求给出的定义都可以用这个收尾："if it would embarrass the team in the retro — that is the thing to flag."}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>One page, four columns.</strong> Decides / delivers / unblocks / must-not-be-surprised — plus the fifth: how they want to be asked.},
q{<strong>One routing question per coffee.</strong> "Who do I ask about X, and how do they want to be asked?" People love answering it — you are asking them to describe their own importance.},
q{<strong>Every node needs a fallback.</strong> "If I am dark, Priya escalates" — maps without fallbacks fail on the first holiday.},
q{<strong>Budget questions go to budget people.</strong> Yesterday\'s mis-route was the tuition; today\'s map is the scholarship.},
q{<strong>"No surprises" is the phrase that rules them all.</strong> Before any demo or decision touching someone\'s domain, ask: would this ambush them?},
],
practice => [
