grammar => [
['One line per decision: the quadruple', q{<em>"Retry policy: three attempts, exponential backoff, dead-letter after — Daniel K, by Thursday."</em> — [decision]: [content] — [owner], by [date]. Four slots, one line, zero ambiguity. The discipline is grammatical: if a decision cannot fit the four slots, it is not yet a decision — it is a discussion.}, q{"Retry policy: three attempts, exponential backoff, dead-letter after — Daniel K, by Thursday."——[决定]：[内容]——[责任人]，by [日期]。四个槽位、一行、零歧义。纪律是语法性的：如果某个决定装不进四个槽位，它还不是决定——只是一场讨论。}],
['Prefixed openness', q{<em>"OPEN — Elena to scope monitoring impact, owner TBD."</em> — the <strong>OPEN</strong> prefix in caps does what italics cannot in email: it makes unfinishedness searchable. Six months later, someone greps the wiki for OPEN items and finds the monitoring scope that never got decided. Prefix grammar is archive grammar.}, q{"OPEN — Elena to scope monitoring impact, owner TBD."——大写的 <strong>OPEN</strong> 前缀完成了邮件里斜体做不到的事：让"未完成"可被检索。六个月后有人检索 wiki 的 OPEN 项，找到那个始终没有决定的监控范围。前缀语法就是归档语法。}],
