tips => [
q{<strong>Type decisions live, not from memory.</strong> The three-list format (decisions / owners / dates) fits in the corner of any screen.},
q{<strong>Half-agreements go to OPEN.</strong> The discipline that separates useful minutes from fiction — record enthusiasm as an open item, never as a decision.},
q{<strong>Send within the hour.</strong> Corrections are cheap while memories are warm; next-day notes get archived uncorrected.},
q{<strong>Invite corrections explicitly.</strong> "I would rather fix a wrong note than archive one" — new joiners get a pass, and every correction is free tuition.},
q{<strong>The owner-date rule is non-negotiable.</strong> A decision without an owner is a wish; a decision without a date is a wish with ambition.},
],
